  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nukala Murall Krishna Murali, vs The State Of A.P, on 18 August, 2020 Author: K. Suresh Reddy Bench: K. Suresh Reddy The Hon'Ble Sri Justice K. Suresh Reddy Criminal Petition No.3173 Of 2020 Order:",
    "facts": "This is a Criminal Petition filed under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure seeking to quash the proceedings in FIR No.190 of 2020, dated 17.06.2020 on the file of I Town Police Station, Kavali, Nellore District registered against the petitioner for the offence punishable under Sections 272, 273, IPC, 59(i), Food Safety and Standards Act and Section 34(A) AP Excise Act.",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the petitioner has placed reliance on the common order dated 18.12.2019 passed by a coordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, holding that \"tobacco\" does not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the Act, therefore, registration of FIR is not permissible.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Counsel for the petitioner has placed reliance on the common order dated 18.12.2019 passed by a coordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, holding that \"tobacco\" does not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the Act, therefore, registration of FIR is not permissible.",
